instructions": "# Quartus Pro Installations on This Workstation\n\nThis file documents the Quartus Prime Pro toolchains installed here.\n\n- **Part A \u2014 Quartus Prime Pro 25.1** (installed 2026-09-22, new)\n- **Part B \u2014 Quartus Pro 26.1.1 and Questa FPGA Edition** (earlier documentation, preserved unchanged)\n\n---\n\n# Part A \u2014 Quartus Prime Pro 25.1 (added September 22, 2026)\n\n## Installation and license\n\n- Installer: `/home/uwb_student00/quartus_25/qinst-linux-25.1-129.run` (Altera unified `qinst` installer)\n- Installation: `/opt/altera/25.1`\n- Quartus: **25.1.0 Build 129, SC Pro Edition** (verified via `quartus_sh --version` with a clean environment)\n- Simulator: **Questa Intel FPGA Edition 2024.3** (`questa_fe`, verified via `vsim -version`)\n- Installed device family: **Agilex 7** (components: `quartus,questa_fe,agilex7`; the installer auto-added `agilex_common` and `quartus_part2`)\n- License file: `/home/uwb_student00/quartus_25/LR-191011_License.dat`\n  - Byte-identical (md5 `13ad95190ee720b3b5d889ecc17ea642`) to `/home/uwb_student00/quartus_26/LR-191011_License.dat`\n  - Node-locked evaluation, expires **December 16, 2026**, tied to NIC MAC `00:be:43:b7:3a:b3`\n- **License activation under 25.1 is NOT yet verified** \u2014 no compile or license checkout has been run against 25.1 as of this writing.\n- Install log: `/home/uwb_student00/quartus_25/install_25.1.log` (\"Installation completed successfully. Total install time: 5 mins 2 secs\")\n- Footprint: 43 GB. Uninstaller: `/opt/altera/25.1/uninstall`\n\n## A.1 Configure your terminal (read the warning first)\n\n**Environment note (updated 2026-09-22):** `~/.bashrc` now defaults to the 25.1 environment (switch approved by Joe; the previous 23.1 block is preserved as comments immediately below the active block, backup at `~/.bashrc.bak-23.1-20260922`). Earlier on install day, `.bashrc` still exported the 23.1 environment, and its `QUARTUS_ROOTDIR_OVERRIDE` redirected even an explicitly invoked 25.1 launcher \u2014 `/opt/altera/25.1/quartus/bin/quartus_sh --version` reported **23.1.0 Build 115** until the override was cleared. Keep this failure mode in mind: any workflow needing a non-default toolchain (e.g., 26.1.1 per Part B) must set its environment explicitly.\n\nRun this before using the 25.1 tools:\n\n```bash\nexport QUARTUS_ROOTDIR_OVERRIDE=/opt/altera/25.1/quartus\nexport PATH=\"/opt/altera/25.1/quartus/bin:/opt/altera/25.1/questa_fe/bin:$PATH\"\n\nexport LM_LICENSE_FILE=\"$HOME/quartus_25/LR-191011_License.dat\"\nexport MGLS_LICENSE_FILE=\"$LM_LICENSE_FILE\"\nexport SALT_LICENSE_SERVER=\"$LM_LICENSE_FILE\"\n```\n\nThe license variables must be **re-pointed** (not just `PATH` prepended) because the inherited 23.1 value references the old `IA-840f` license file.\n\nAs with Questa under 26.1.1, `SALT_LICENSE_SERVER` is required by the Questa FPGA Edition license check.\n\nVerify tool selection:\n\n```bash\ncommand -v quartus_sh && quartus_sh --version   # expect: Version 25.1.0 Build 129 SC Pro Edition\ncommand -v vsim && vsim -version                # expect: Questa Intel FPGA Edition-64 2024.3\n```\n\n### Shell default (changed 2026-09-22, Joe-approved)\n\n`~/.bashrc` now exports the 25.1 environment as the login default (license vars, `QUARTUS_ROOTDIR_OVERRIDE`, `PATH`). The previous 23.1 block is **preserved as comments** directly below the active block \u2014 to revert, comment the 25.1 block, uncomment the 23.1 block, then:\n\n```bash\nsource ~/.bashrc\nhash -r\n```\n\nA fresh login shell was verified after the switch: `quartus_sh --version` \u2192 25.1.0 Build 129, `vsim -version` \u2192 Questa 2024.3, and `LM_LICENSE_FILE`/`MGLS_LICENSE_FILE`/`SALT_LICENSE_SERVER` all pointing at `~/quartus_25/LR-191011_License.dat`. Workflows expecting the 26.1.1 environment from Part B must now set it explicitly.\n\n## A.2 Use Quartus 25.1\n\nSame command-line flow as Part B section 2:\n\n```bash\nquartus_sh --flow compile my_project          # or: -c my_revision\n```\n\nReports and timing results land in the project's configured output directory (commonly `output_files/`). **Nothing has been compiled under 25.1 yet** \u2014 first-use license checkout is untested.\n\n## A.3 Use Questa 2024.3\n\nSame flow as Part B section 3 (`vlib work`, `vlog -sv ...`, `vsim -c work.tb -do 'run -all; quit -f'`). Launch from a terminal configured per A.1 so the license variables are inherited.\n\n## A.4 Verification status for 25.1 (September 22, 2026)\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Install via `qinst` (quartus, questa_fe, agilex7) | Completed successfully, 5 mins 2 secs |\n| `quartus_sh --version` (clean environment) | 25.1.0 Build 129 SC Pro Edition |\n| `vsim -version` | Questa Intel FPGA Edition-64 2024.3 (2024.09, Sep 10 2024) |\n| License file present and identical to 26.1.1 copy | Yes (md5 `13ad9519\u2026`) |\n| License checkout under 25.1 | Not verified |\n| Synthesis / fit / timing under 25.1 | Not performed |\n| JTAG visibility / board operation | Not attempted |\n\nContext: the OFS `ofs-2025.1-1` release notes list **Quartus Prime Pro 25.1 (patches: None)** as the validated toolchain for that release family.\n\n## Troubleshooting (25.1)\n\n### `quartus_sh` reports 23.1 (Version 23.1.0 Build 115)\n\nThe `QUARTUS_ROOTDIR_OVERRIDE` from `~/.bashrc` is active in your shell. Re-export the full A.1 block \u2014 setting `PATH` alone is not enough \u2014 or bypass the environment for a one-off check:\n\n```bash\nenv -u QUARTUS_ROOTDIR_OVERRIDE /opt/altera/25.1/quartus/bin/quartus_sh --version\n```\n\n### Questa reports an invalid license environment\n\nSame checks as Part B: `printenv LM_LICENSE_FILE MGLS_LICENSE_FILE SALT_LICENSE_SERVER` \u2014 all three must reference the `~/quartus_25/LR-191011_License.dat` file, not the old `IA-840f` one inherited from `~/.bashrc`.\n\n---\n\n# Part B \u2014 Quartus Pro 26.1.1 and Questa FPGA Edition\n\n*(Documentation from the 26.1.1 installation, preserved unchanged. A backup of the original file is at `instructions.md.bak-26.1.1-20260922`.)*\n\n## Installation and license\n\n- Installation: `/opt/altera/26.1.1`\n- Quartus: **26.1.1 Build 130, Pro Edition**\n- Simulator: **Questa Altera FPGA Edition 2025.3** (`questa_fe`)\n- Installed device family: **Agilex 7**\n- License: `/home/uwb_student00/quartus_26/LR-191011_License.dat`\n- License expiration: **December 16, 2026**\n- License type: node-locked evaluation, tied to this workstation's NIC MAC address `00:be:43:b7:3a:b3`.\n\nThe license includes Quartus Standard/Pro and Questa FPGA Edition. Renew or replace the license before it expires.\n\n## 1. Configure your terminal\n\nRun this before using the tools:\n\n```bash\nexport QUARTUS_ROOTDIR_OVERRIDE=/opt/altera/26.1.1/quartus\nexport PATH=\"/opt/altera/26.1.1/quartus/bin:/opt/altera/26.1.1/questa_fe/bin:$PATH\"\n\nexport LM_LICENSE_FILE=\"$HOME/quartus_26/LR-191011_License.dat\"\nexport MGLS_LICENSE_FILE=\"$LM_LICENSE_FILE\"\nexport SALT_LICENSE_SERVER=\"$LM_LICENSE_FILE\"\n```\n\n**Important:** This Questa release requires `SALT_LICENSE_SERVER`. During verification, simulation failed with only `LM_LICENSE_FILE` and `MGLS_LICENSE_FILE`, then passed after setting `SALT_LICENSE_SERVER` to the license file.\n\n### Make the settings persistent\n\nEdit `~/.bashrc` and replace the old Quartus/license exports with the block above. At verification time, the old settings referenced:\n\n- `/opt/intelFPGA_pro/23.1/quartus`\n- `/opt/intelFPGA_pro/23.1/questa_fe`\n- `/home/uwb_student00/IA-840f/LR-157262_License.dat`\n\nIn particular, an old `QUARTUS_ROOTDIR_OVERRIDE` redirects even an explicitly invoked new Quartus launcher to the old installation.\n\nAfter saving, open a new terminal or run:\n\n```bash\nsource ~/.bashrc\nhash -r\n```\n\nVerify tool selection:\n\n```bash\ncommand -v quartus_sh\nquartus_sh --version\ncommand -v vsim\nvsim -version\n```\n\nExpected versions: Quartus **26.1.1 Build 130** and Questa FPGA Edition **2025.3**. Run development tools as your normal user; root is not needed for license checkout, compilation, or simulation.\n\n## 2. Use Quartus\n\n### Graphical interface\n\nFrom a desktop terminal with a working display:\n\n```bash\nquartus\n```\n\nOpen your project's `.qpf` file. GUI operation was not verified in the headless SSH session.\n\n### Command-line compilation\n\nFrom the directory containing your project, substitute its actual name for `my_project`:\n\n```bash\nquartus_sh --flow compile my_project\n```\n\nFor a specific revision:\n\n```bash\nquartus_sh --flow compile my_project -c my_revision\n```\n\nCheck the compilation reports and timing results in the project's configured output directory, commonly `output_files/`. Before programming a real board, use its correct FPGA part, pin assignments, timing constraints, Reset Release IP, and power-management settings.\n\n## 3. Use Questa FPGA Edition\n\nFrom your simulation working directory, compile your design and testbench. Replace the example filenames and top-level testbench name with your own:\n\n```bash\nvlib work\nvlog -sv design.sv testbench.sv\nvsim -c work.tb -do 'run -all; quit -f'\n```\n\nCreate `work` only if it does not already exist. For VHDL, compile sources using `vcom` instead of `vlog`.\n\nThe testbench should terminate or otherwise stop the simulation after checking its results. Inspect the transcript for errors and assertion failures; for automated testing, make the testbench/script return a nonzero exit code on failure.\n\nFor interactive graphical simulation with a working display:\n\n```bash\nvsim work.tb\n```\n\nFor designs containing Altera IP, use the IP/project-generated simulation setup scripts and required simulation libraries, rather than only compiling the top-level HDL files.\n\n## 4. Check programming hardware\n\n```bash\njtagconfig\nquartus_pgm --list\n```\n\nAt verification time, both reported **No JTAG hardware available**. Connect and power the board and its supported JTAG connection, then repeat these checks. If a cable is attached but not visible, investigate USB visibility, cable drivers/permissions, and JTAG server configuration.\n\nFrom a graphical desktop, launch the programmer with:\n\n```bash\nquartus_pgm\n```\n\nSelect the correct hardware and a programming file built for the actual board. Hardware programming and board functionality have not yet been verified.\n\n## 5. Verification performed on September 17, 2026\n\nThe following checks used the installation and license paths documented above:\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Quartus version | 26.1.1 Build 130 |\n| Agilex 7 device database | Installed; 2,811 device entries |\n| Small counter synthesis | Passed |\n| Placement and routing | Passed; zero errors or warnings |\n| Timing analysis at 100 MHz | Passed; setup slack +7.284 ns, hold slack +0.124 ns |\n| Assembler/programming-file generation | Passed; generated `smoke.sof` |\n| Questa FPGA Edition simulation | Passed; counter reached expected value 10; zero errors |\n| JTAG visibility | No hardware detected |\n| GUI and real-board operation | Not verified |\n\nThe compile test targeted `AGIA027R31A1E1VC` with virtual I/O pins. It generated warnings about missing Reset Release IP and board-specific power-management settings. **Its `smoke.sof` is a toolchain test artifact, not a programming file for the workstation's board.**\n\nVerification sources and reports were left in `/tmp/opencode/altera_verify/`, including:\n\n- `smoke.sv`: counter and self-checking testbench\n- `compile.tcl` and `smoke.sdc`: Quartus test setup\n- `compile.log`: synthesis, fitting, and timing results\n- `assembler.log`: successful standalone assembler run\n- `transcript`: Questa simulation output\n- `output_files/`: Quartus reports and test programming file\n\nThe full-flow command reached the execution time limit after timing analysis; the assembler was then run separately and completed successfully. Temporary files may be removed by system cleanup.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Quartus reports version 23.1\n\nCheck `QUARTUS_ROOTDIR_OVERRIDE` and `PATH`, then reapply the environment block in section 1. An absolute path to the new launcher alone does not override an old `QUARTUS_ROOTDIR_OVERRIDE`.\n\n### Questa reports an invalid license environment\n\nVerify:\n\n```bash\nprintenv LM_LICENSE_FILE MGLS_LICENSE_FILE SALT_LICENSE_SERVER\ntest -r \"$SALT_LICENSE_SERVER\" && printf 'License file is readable\\n'\n```\n\nAll three variables should reference the current `LR-191011_License.dat` file. Launch Questa from the configured terminal so it inherits these settings.\n\n### License checkout fails after previously working\n\nCheck the error message, license expiration, system date, file readability, and workstation host-ID match. This license expires December 16, 2026 and is tied to this machine. Installing the software on another host does not transfer the license.\n"}
